From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:19:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 31/31] board: mediatek-mobile: forward the boot framebuffer as
 no-map

LK reserves its framebuffer without no-map. Forwarded as is, the OS keeps
it in its linear map, and arm64 refuses to ioremap that RAM, so a
simple-framebuffer driver cannot take over the panel. Mark reservations
that overlap the framebuffer no-map in the OS FDT.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 board/mediatek/mediatek-mobile/mediatek-mobile.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/board/mediatek/mediatek-mobile/mediatek-mobile.c b/board/mediatek/mediatek-mobile/mediatek-mobile.c
index 1b637e882c1..ae76e966dad 100644
--- a/board/mediatek/mediatek-mobile/mediatek-mobile.c
+++ b/board/mediatek/mediatek-mobile/mediatek-mobile.c
@@ -1032,7 +1032,12 @@ int ft_board_setup(void *blob, struct bd_info *bd)
 		if (node < 0)
 			return node;
 		ret = fdt_setprop(blob, node, "reg", reg, sizeof(reg));
-		if (!ret && r->nomap)
+		/*
+		 * LK keeps its framebuffer mapped; the OS must not, so that a
+		 * simple-framebuffer driver can map the scanout buffer.
+		 */
+		if (!ret && (r->nomap ||
+			     mtk_overlaps(r->start, r->size, mtk_fb_start, mtk_fb_size)))
 			ret = fdt_setprop_empty(blob, node, "no-map");
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
